{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "label": "GLUE: how it works now", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One place that says how GLUE works today; ADRs say why. Must stay true after each change that alters how GLUE works."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_folder", "label": "The GLUE folder (JSON files, no database)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The user's data is JSON files in the GLUE folder, no database (ADR 0009). Lowercase mco names are real file and setting names; data depends on them, so they stay."}, {"id": "vault_system_shared_collections", "label": "Shared form: one copy of a collection in GLUE Cloud", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With cloud sync on, every collection is the account's, one copy in GLUE Cloud, with each computer's songs and analyses stored per computer (ADRs 0101, 0112, 0130)."}, {"id": "vault_system_one_id_per_computer", "label": "One id per computer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only a computer's own GLUE folder writes its parts of a shared collection; nothing is written under an unknown or stand-in id (ADRs 0108, 0158)."}, {"id": "vault_system_sync", "label": "Shared sync: snapshot and log", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pushes are one log entry each; the device pulls, merges per field (merge3) and pushes again. Clashes wait in a box, and a computer never clashes with itself (ADRs 0106, 0095, 0163). Shared sync is in Rust in GLUE Home (ADR 0155)."}, {"id": "vault_system_local_link", "label": "GLUE Home local link on 127.0.0.1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GLUE Home answers on 127.0.0.1 ports 47400-47409; every route but hello and connect needs the token. Any browser on the computer can take the link (ADRs 0048, 0115)."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_home_engine", "label": "GLUE Home engine (Rust)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GLUE Home's engine does the library work: stores, edits, jobs, repair, analysis queue, sync, DJ libraries, duplicates; the page is its screen (ADRs 0153, 0154, 0160)."}, {"id": "vault_system_home_mode", "label": "Home mode: the page is only GLUE Home's screen", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With GLUE Home running, the website reads the GLUE folder over the local link and runs none of the library work itself (ADRs 0051, 0162)."}, {"id": "vault_system_writer_lease", "label": "Writer lease for the GLUE folder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One writer of the GLUE folder at a time: a tab in Home mode writes only while it holds GLUE Home's lease; GLUE Home writes only while no lease is held (ADR 0051)."}, {"id": "vault_system_analysis_in_engine", "label": "Analysis in GLUE Home's engine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One pipeline in songs-at-a-time order: songs asked for now, new songs' tags, the library's songs, then thumbnails. Passing failures are retried, never stored; a song that fails three times is saved as failed (ADRs 0157, 0109, 0144). No audio JavaScript remains (ADR 0147)."}, {"id": "vault_system_dj_libraries_in_rust", "label": "DJ libraries read in Rust (glue-interop)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rekordbox, Traktor, Apple Music, Serato, Engine DJ and M3U are read by crates/glue-interop, held byte for byte to the website's parsers (ADR 0167). The main library is one per computer (ADR 0169)."}, {"id": "vault_system_engine_dj_two_way", "label": "Engine DJ kept in step both ways", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cues, loops, grids and song info are merged three ways against the last agreed values; Engine DJ's database is written only while Engine DJ is closed, after a backup (ADRs 0170, 0172, 0173, 0179, 0180, 0181)."}, {"id": "vault_system_cues_loops_every_app", "label": "Cues, loops and beat grids from every DJ app", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each DJ library record keeps its cues and grid; GLUE writes into a DJ app's library only as ADR 0168 allows: through GLUE Home, opt-in, backup first, app closed."}, {"id": "vault_system_streaming_webrtc", "label": "Streaming to other devices over WebRTC", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Songs go between the user's own computers over WebRTC, signaled through GLUE Cloud; GLUE Cloud never carries audio except via the TURN relay (ADRs 0150, 0174, 0175, 0176, 0037)."}, {"id": "vault_system_signaling_room", "label": "Signaling room (per-account Durable Object)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Presence and WebRTC signals per account; a silent socket is let go after 150 s, and a room silent for 75 s is reconnected (ADRs 0158, 0132)."}, {"id": "vault_system_duplicates", "label": "Duplicates matched and grouped by GLUE Home", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fingerprints and name matching; the best copy is chosen by quality and kept; GLUE Home does the matching where it runs (ADRs 0164, 0165, 0120, 0121, 0117)."}, {"id": "vault_system_relink_no_file", "label": "No file linked: relinking songs with no file", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A DJ library's record with no file is matched to a library song with certainty, and linked, keeping its playlists (ADR 0124)."}, {"id": "vault_system_verdicts", "label": "Quality verdicts (Speklone forensics)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A hi-res file is judged by what reaches past 24 kHz; a steep top end with content above it is a lowpass in the master (ADRs 0116, 0119). Stored verdicts are judged again from kept details when VERDICT_VERSION changes (ADR 0166)."}, {"id": "vault_system_caches", "label": "Caches outside the GLUE folder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Details, thumbnails, waveforms and covers are caches, not GLUE's data; GLUE Home tidies its cache daily, leaving alone what it can't read (ADR 0185)."}, {"id": "vault_system_profiles", "label": "Profiles are artist aliases", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A profile is an artist alias with a colour and BPM range; a GLUE folder has one library that every alias opens (ADRs 0113, 0114). Signed in, the account keeps the union of every device's profiles."}, {"id": "vault_system_gluey_guide", "label": "Gluey: tours and help articles", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tours are data pointing at data-guide parts of the UI; help articles are src/help markdown; the first tour shows once per person (ADR 0126)."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_cloud_component", "label": "GLUE Cloud (Cloudflare Worker, D1, Durable Object)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Optional account service: keeps collections (never music), profiles and devices; no library data or audio. Runs the signaling room and TURN credentials (ADRs 0036, 0091)."}, {"id": "src_core_shared_project", "label": "src/core/shared/project.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_store_shared_engine", "label": "src/store/shared/engine.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_store_collection", "label": "src/store/collection.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "crates_glue_engine_src_sync", "label": "crates/glue-engine/src/sync.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "crates_glue_engine_src_shared", "label": "crates/glue-engine/src/shared.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "crates_glue_engine_src_room", "label": "crates/glue-engine/src/room.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "crates_glue_engine_src_queue", "label": "crates/glue-engine/src/queue.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "crates_glue_engine_src_dupes", "label": "crates/glue-engine/src/dupes.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "home_src_tauri_src_local", "label": "home/src-tauri/src/local.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "home_src_tauri_src_rtc", "label": "home/src-tauri/src/rtc.rs", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_platform_homedisk", "l